@startuml
title HIP-4 — converting between quote tokens and outcome shares
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ComponentFontColor #1F3A5F
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1F3A5F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

package "A standalone outcome" {
  [X quote tokens] as Q1
  [X Yes  +  X No] as YN
  Q1 -right-> YN : splitOutcome
  YN -left-> Q1 : mergeOutcome
}

package "A question: outcomes A, B and the fallback,\nexactly one of which settles Yes" {
  [X Yes(A) + X Yes(B) + X Yes(fallback)] as ALLY
  [X quote tokens] as Q2
  [X No(A)] as NOA
  [X Yes(B) + X Yes(fallback)] as OTHERY
  ALLY -right-> Q2 : mergeQuestion
  NOA -right-> OTHERY : negateOutcome
}

note bottom of YN
  Settlement pays settleFraction per Yes share and
  1 - settleFraction per No share, so the two sides of
  an outcome always sum to exactly one quote token.
  Nothing can become undercollateralised, which is why
  outcome markets have no leverage and no liquidations.
end note

note bottom of NOA
  negateOutcome lets a holder who is short one outcome
  redeem before settlement: "not A" is the same claim as
  "B or the fallback" once the question is exhaustive.
end note
@enduml
